## Introduction

The MedSync API enables healthcare organizations to integrate with MedSync products programmatically. This document provides an overview of API capabilities, authentication, and usage patterns.

---

## API Basics

### Base URLs

| Environment | URL |
|-------------|-----|
| Production | https://api.medsync.health/v2 |
| Sandbox | https://api-sandbox.medsync.health/v2 |
| US-East (DR) | https://api-east.medsync.health/v2 |

### Authentication

All API requests require authentication using OAuth 2.0.

**Supported Flows**:
- Client Credentials (server-to-server)
- Authorization Code (user-context)
- SMART on FHIR (EHR-launched)

**Token Endpoint**: `https://auth.medsync.health/oauth/token`

**Example Request**:
```http
POST /oauth/token HTTP/1.1
Host: auth.medsync.health
Content-Type: application/x-www-form-urlencoded

grant_type=client_credentials&
client_id=YOUR_CLIENT_ID&
client_secret=YOUR_CLIENT_SECRET&
scope=patients.read tasks.write
```

**Token Lifetime**: 1 hour (refresh tokens: 30 days)

